    "ts": "2026-08-05T09:14:23+00:00",
    "headline": "Crypto Weekly: Coinbase feels crypto squeeze, South Africa's new rules",
    "summary": "<body><p>STORY: From crypto giants feeling the squeeze to South Africa's new crypto rules...</p><p>This is Crypto Weekly.</p><p>:: Crypto Weekly</p><p>:: Coinbase posts third straight quarterly loss</p><p>Coinbase posted a third straight quarterly loss.</p><p>The crypto giant saw a drop of close to $360 million for the quarter ended June 30 - well down from a profit of $1.43 billion a year earlier.</p><p>Crypto markets came under pressure during the April-to-June quarter.</p><p>Investors turned away from riskier assets due to uncertainty over U.S. interest rates, geopolitical tensions and outflows from crypto investment products.</p><p>:: Trump-backed American Bitcoin swings to quarterly loss</p><p>American Bitcoin was another company to feel the mood sour around crypto.</p><p>The bitcoin miner is backed by two of U.S. President Donald Trump's sons.</p><p>Its net loss hit just over $57 million as bitcoin prices slid 11% from April to June.</p><p>:: South Africa drafts new crypto rules</p><p>South Africa took a step closer to bringing crypto into its financial rulebook.</p><p>The country released draft guidelines for the first time on&nbsp;when moving crypto across borders becomes a regulated and reportable event.</p><p>The draft Crypto Asset Manual was published jointly by the National Treasury and the South African Reserve Bank, and comes as crypto use widens in the country.</p><p>:: Robinhood Markets sees weakness in crypto trading</p><p>And Robinhood Markets beat Wall Street estimates for second-quarter profit.</p><p>It saw strong trading in equities, options and prediction markets, but weakness in crypto trading.</p><p>Analysts argue the quick expansion of prediction markets has turned investor focus away from crypto.</p><p>And market watchers now expect the prediction sector to play an even more key role in Robinhood's revenue mix.</p></body>",
    "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/video/crypto-weekly-coinbase-feels-crypto-091423264.html",
    "source": "Reuters Videos",
    "provider": "yfinance",
    "raw": {
      "id": "68fbac50-5a62-31a3-b95e-1a32d5924950",
      "content": {
        "id": "68fbac50-5a62-31a3-b95e-1a32d5924950",
        "contentType": "VIDEO",
        "title": "Crypto Weekly: Coinbase feels crypto squeeze, South Africa's new rules",
        "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: From crypto giants feeling the squeeze to South Africa's new crypto rules...</p><p>This is Crypto Weekly.</p><p>:: Crypto Weekly</p><p>:: Coinbase posts third straight quarterly loss</p><p>Coinbase posted a third straight quarterly loss.</p><p>The crypto giant saw a drop of close to $360 million for the quarter ended June 30 - well down from a profit of $1.43 billion a year earlier.</p><p>Crypto markets came under pressure during the April-to-June quarter.</p><p>Investors turned away from riskier assets due to uncertainty over U.S. interest rates, geopolitical tensions and outflows from crypto investment products.</p><p>:: Trump-backed American Bitcoin swings to quarterly loss</p><p>American Bitcoin was another company to feel the mood sour around crypto.</p><p>The bitcoin miner is backed by two of U.S. President Donald Trump's sons.</p><p>Its net loss hit just over $57 million as bitcoin prices slid 11% from April to June.</p><p>:: South Africa drafts new crypto rules</p><p>South Africa took a step closer to bringing crypto into its financial rulebook.</p><p>The country released draft guidelines for the first time on when moving crypto across borders becomes a regulated and reportable event.</p><p>The draft Crypto Asset Manual was published jointly by the National Treasury and the South African Reserve Bank, and comes as crypto use widens in the country.</p><p>:: Robinhood Markets sees weakness in crypto trading</p><p>And Robinhood Markets beat Wall Street estimates for second-quarter profit.</p><p>It saw strong trading in equities, options and prediction markets, but weakness in crypto trading.</p><p>Analysts argue the quick expansion of prediction markets has turned investor focus away from crypto.</p><p>And market watchers now expect the prediction sector to play an even more key role in Robinhood's revenue mix.</p></body></title>",
